{"seq":2,"at":"2026-10-20","kind":"edited","target":{"type":"article","id":"a2110"},"reason":"Rewritten by the merge to take in the printed cards' questions.","by":"merge geography/physical","ref":"quiz-archive/runs/tp-ingest/decisions/geography__physical.g2.json","changes":[{"field":"bodyEn","diff":[["=",390],["-","China,"],["+","China;"],["=",1],["+","with around 35 kilograms of sediment in every cubic metre of water, the Yellow River (Huang He) is the muddiest of the world's great rivers. The Chinese call it the \"Mother River\", "],["=",54],["+","Its course has wandered across the North China Plain again and again; the first recorded great shift came in 602 BC. "],["=",811]]},{"field":"bodyDe","diff":[["=",326],["-","mitführt,"],["+","mitführt;"],["=",1],["+","mit rund 35 Kilogramm Schwebstoffen in jedem Kubikmeter Wasser ist der Strom – kurz Gelber Fluss (Huang He) genannt – der schlammigste der großen Ströme der Welt. Die Chinesen nennen ihn den „Mutterfluss“, "],["=",56],["+","Sein Lauf ist immer wieder über die Nordchinesische Ebene gewandert; die erste überlieferte große Laufverlagerung fand 602 v. Chr. statt. "],["=",749]]}]},
