{"seq":7,"at":"2026-10-21","kind":"edited","target":{"type":"article","id":"a2110"},"reason":"Proofread (reasons in the entries above / the batch report).","by":"enrich batch 083","ref":"quiz-archive/runs/tp-enrich/enrich-report/a1810-a2327.md","changes":[{"field":"bodyEn","diff":[["=",396],["-","35"],["+","34"],["=",25],["-","(Huang He) "],["=",250],["-","4,350"],["+","4,350–4,900"],["=",219],["-","Sea;"],["+","Sea."],["=",1],["-","since"],["+","At"],["=",1],["+","an estimated 4,350 to 4,900 kilometres, depending on the source, it is longer than the Mississippi, and on its way it passes through six countries: China, Myanmar, Laos, Thailand, Cambodia and Vietnam. Since "],["=",166],["-","Pakistan."],["+","Pakistan,"],["=",1],["+","until India suspended it in April 2025. "],["=",242],["+","fringed by "],["=",2],["+","mangrove forests of the "],["=",51]]},{"field":"bodyDe","diff":[["=",332],["-","35"],["+","34"],["=",17],["-","Strom"],["+","„Gelber"],["=",1],["-","–"],["+","Fluss“"],["=",1],["-","kurz"],["+","genannte"],["=",1],["-","Gelber"],["+","Strom"],["=",1],["-","Fluss (Huang He) genannt – "],["=",230],["-","4.350"],["+","4.350–4.900"],["=",211],["-","erreicht;"],["+","erreicht."],["=",1],["-","seit"],["+","Mit"],["=",1],["+","geschätzten 4.350 bis 4.900 Kilometern, je nach Quelle, ist er länger als der Mississippi und durchquert auf seinem Weg sechs Länder: China, Myanmar, Laos, Thailand, Kambodscha und Vietnam. Seit "],["=",144],["-","auf."],["+","auf,"],["=",1],["+","bis Indien ihn im April 2025 aussetzte. "],["=",226],["-","die"],["+","gesäumt"],["=",1],["+","von den Mangrovenwäldern der "],["=",51]]},{"field":"notesEn","old":"Answer also accepted as Chang Jiang and Huang He.","new":"The Yangtze is also accepted as Chang Jiang, the Yellow River as Huang He."},{"field":"notesDe","old":"Als Antwort gelten auch Jangtse / Chang Jiang und Huang He (Hwangho).","new":"Als Antwort gelten auch Jangtse / Chang Jiang für den Jangtsekiang und Huang He (Hwangho) für den